     NUM("Monthly mean temperatures: the highest is 27 °C and the lowest is 23 °C. What is the annual range in °C?", 4, "27 − 23 = 4 °C.", unit="°C"),
     MCQ("Heavy afternoon showers in the equatorial region are mainly", "Convectional rainfall", ["Frontal rainfall", "Relief rainfall only", "Snowfall"], "Strong heating makes air rise, cool and condense."),
     OPEN("Describe how relief rainfall occurs.", "Moist air is blown towards a mountain and forced to rise over it. As it rises it cools, the water vapour condenses into clouds and rain falls on the windward slope. The leeward side is drier because the air sinks and warms (rain shadow).", "2 marks for forced uplift and cooling; 2 marks for condensation and rain on the windward side; 1 mark for rain shadow.", points=5),
