    [("text", "**Population density** is the average number of people per square kilometre: total population ÷ area. **Birth rate** and **death rate** are the numbers of births and deaths per 1 000 people in a year. **Natural increase** = birth rate − death rate (per 1 000). If it is positive, the population grows."),
     ("key", "retenir", "Distribution of population", "People live where life is easier: fertile soil, reliable water, mild climate, flat land, jobs, trade routes and good services. They avoid steep mountains, dense forest, dry desert and swamps. In Cameroon the western highlands, the coast around Douala and the area around Yaoundé are densely populated, while the East and parts of the Adamawa plateau have fewer people per km²."),
     ("text", "**Migration** is the movement of people from one place to live in another. **Push factors** make people leave (unemployment, poor services, drought, conflict, floods). **Pull factors** attract them (jobs, schools, hospitals, electricity, safety). **Rural-urban migration** is very common in Cameroon. Effects: towns grow rapidly and may lack housing and jobs, while villages may lose young workers."),
     ("text", "A **settlement** is a place where people live. Patterns: **nucleated** (houses grouped together), **dispersed** (scattered houses) and **linear** (along a road or river). Settlements have functions such as farming, market, administration, industry, port or tourism. **Site** is the exact land a settlement occupies; **situation** is its position in relation to other places."),
     ("key", "attention", "Urban problems and solutions", "Rapid growth can lead to overcrowding, slums, traffic jams, unemployment, pollution, waste and flooding. Solutions include planned housing, better public transport, waste collection, drainage, developing rural areas to reduce migration, and creating jobs.")],
    [("Example 1: population density", "A district has 600 000 people and an area of 1 200 km². Calculate the population density.", ["Density = population ÷ area.", "Density = 600 000 ÷ 1 200.", "600 000 ÷ 1 200 = 500."], "500 people per km²."),
     ("Example 2: natural increase", "A country has a birth rate of 35 per 1 000 and a death rate of 10 per 1 000. Find the natural increase per 1 000 and say what happens to the population.", ["Natural increase = 35 − 10.", "35 − 10 = 25 per 1 000.", "The result is positive, so the population grows (by about 2.5% a year)."], "25 per 1 000 (2.5%); the population is growing.")],
    (fig, "Push and pull factors in rural-urban migration", "Two boxes, rural area and town, joined by an arrow showing migration, with push and pull factors."),
