L = lesson(c4, "industry-energy", "Industry and energy",
    ["Classify economic activities as primary, secondary and tertiary", "Explain factors affecting the location of industries", "Describe the main sources of energy and their advantages", "Give Cameroonian examples"],
    [("text", "Economic activities are grouped in three sectors. **Primary** activities take natural resources (farming, fishing, mining, logging). **Secondary** activities process or manufacture (food processing, brewing, cement, sawmills). **Tertiary** activities are services (trade, banking, transport, teaching, health, tourism)."),
     ("key", "retenir", "Location of industries", "Industries are placed where costs are low and profit is high: **raw materials**, **power**, **labour**, **market**, **transport** (roads, railway, port), **capital** (money), **water** and **government policy**. Many industries in Cameroon are at Douala, which has the main port, a large market and good roads and rail. Edea, near the Sanaga, has an aluminium factory that uses hydroelectric power."),
     ("text", "Energy sources are **non-renewable** (oil, natural gas, coal) because they will run out, or **renewable** (water, sun, wind, biomass), because they are replaced naturally. **Hydroelectric power** is the most important source of electricity in Cameroon, with dams on the Sanaga (Song Loulou, Edea) and the Benue (Lagdo). Oil and gas are produced offshore. Fuelwood is widely used for cooking."),
     ("key", "retenir", "Advantages and disadvantages", "- Hydro: renewable and cheap to run, but dams are expensive and depend on rainfall.\n- Oil and gas: valuable exports, but pollute and may run out.\n- Solar: clean and useful for remote villages, but depends on sunshine and has high set-up costs.\n- Fuelwood: cheap, but causes deforestation."),
     ("key", "attention", "Be careful", "- Industry is not only factories: the tertiary sector is also an economic activity.\n- 'Renewable' does not mean 'free of problems': dams change rivers and flood land.\n- Always link a factory's location to at least two factors in your answer.")],
    [("Example 1: classify", "Classify: A) cutting timber in the forest; B) sawing timber into planks at a mill in Douala; C) selling planks in a shop.", ["Cutting timber takes a natural resource: primary.", "Sawing is processing: secondary.", "Selling is a service: tertiary."], "A primary, B secondary, C tertiary."),
     ("Example 2: location factors", "Give two reasons why an aluminium smelter is located at Edea.", ["Smelting uses a great deal of electricity, so a nearby power source is vital.", "Edea is near the Sanaga hydroelectric power and close to Douala port for importing materials and exporting aluminium.", "The two main factors are power and transport."], "Hydroelectric power and good transport links.")],
    (fig, "The three sectors of the economy", "Three boxes showing primary, secondary and tertiary activities with examples."),
    [MCQ("Which of these is a secondary activity?", "Making cement", ["Fishing", "Teaching", "Cutting timber"], "Manufacturing and processing are secondary."),
     TF("Hydroelectric power is a renewable source of energy.", True, "Flowing water is replaced by rain."),
     MATCH("Match the sector to an example.", [("Primary", "Mining"), ("Secondary", "Brewery"), ("Tertiary", "Banking")], "Raw materials, manufacture and service.", tier="application"),
     MCQ("A likely reason for a factory at Douala is", "The port and large market", ["No electricity", "Far from roads", "No workers"], "Douala has many advantages for industry.", tier="approfondissement"),
     OPEN("State two disadvantages of fuelwood as an energy source.", "It causes deforestation and soil erosion, produces smoke that harms health, and takes time to collect.", "1 mark each for two valid disadvantages with brief reason.", points=2, tier="approfondissement"),
     PROB("A company plans to build a fruit-juice factory. Fruit is grown in the surrounding villages. The main customers are in a large town 60 km away.",
          [("mcq", "Which factor strongly favours the site?", "Raw materials nearby", ["No road to the town", "No labour", "No water"], "Fruit nearby cuts transport costs.", {}),
           ("tf", "Juice making belongs to the secondary sector.", True, "It processes fruit into a product.", {}),
           ("mcq", "Which energy source would be a good back-up in a village without grid electricity?", "Solar power", ["Nuclear power", "Coal-fired plant", "A volcano"], "Solar suits sunny places without a grid.", {}),
           ("open", "Give two benefits of the factory for the villages.", "Jobs, a market for farmers' fruit, higher incomes, growth of services and better roads.", "1 mark each for two benefits.", {})])],
    [("Which of these is non-renewable?", "Crude oil", ["Sunlight", "Flowing water", "Wind"], "Oil forms over millions of years and will run out."),
     ("The Lagdo dam is on the river", "Benue", ["Sanaga", "Wouri", "Nyong"], "Lagdo is on the Benue in the north."),
     ("An example of a tertiary activity is", "Teaching", ["Mining", "Farming", "Making cement"], "Services are tertiary."),
     ("Aluminium smelters need large amounts of", "Electricity", ["Snow", "Wind only", "Cotton"], "Smelting is very energy-hungry."),
     ("A raw material for a sawmill is", "Logs", ["Plastic", "Bread", "Steel"], "A sawmill processes timber.")],
    ["Teacher to verify: Edea aluminium plant and Sanaga dams (Song Loulou, Edea), Lagdo dam on the Benue, offshore oil and gas; and that hydro is the main source of electricity in Cameroon."])

