L = lesson(c5, "cameroon-physical", "Cameroon: location, relief, climate, rivers and vegetation",
    ["Locate Cameroon and name its neighbours and regions", "Describe the main relief regions", "Describe the climates, rivers and vegetation of Cameroon in their regional pattern"],
    [("text", "Cameroon lies in Central Africa on the Gulf of Guinea, between Nigeria to the west and Chad, the Central African Republic, the Congo, Gabon and Equatorial Guinea to the east and south. It is shaped like a triangle with its apex at Lake Chad in the north and its base on the Atlantic coast. It covers about 475 000 km². The capital is Yaoundé and the economic capital is Douala. The country has **ten regions**: Adamawa, Centre, East, Far North, Littoral, North, North West, South, South West and West."),
     ("key", "retenir", "Relief regions", "- **Coastal plain:** low, hot and wet, with mangroves and sandy and muddy shores.\n- **Southern plateau:** a forested plateau, about 650 m high, that covers much of the Centre, South and East.\n- **Western highlands:** volcanic mountains such as Mount Cameroon, Manengouba, Bamboutos and Oku, with fertile soils and cooler climate.\n- **Adamawa plateau:** a high plateau, around 1 000 m, in the centre.\n- **Northern lowlands:** the Benue basin and the Chad basin, with the Mandara Mountains in the Far North."),
     ("text", "Cameroon is often called **Africa in miniature** because it contains most of Africa's landscapes and climates: equatorial forest, savanna, desert-edge Sahel, mountains and coast. In the south the **equatorial climate** brings heavy rain with two rainy seasons; the coast and Mount Cameroon slopes receive very heavy rain in a long wet season; the **Adamawa and western highlands** are cooler; the north has a **tropical** (Sudanian) climate and the Far North a **Sahelian** climate with a short rainy season."),
     ("key", "retenir", "Rivers and vegetation", "Rivers flowing to the Atlantic: the **Sanaga** (the longest river wholly in Cameroon), **Wouri**, **Nyong**, **Ntem** and **Mungo**. Rivers flowing to the interior basins: the **Benue** (towards the Niger), the **Logone** (towards Lake Chad) and the **Sangha** system in the south-east (towards the Congo basin). Vegetation changes from rainforest and mangroves in the south, to savanna with scattered trees in the centre and north, and thorn steppe in the Far North."),
     ("key", "pieges", "Common mistakes", "- Cameroon does not have one single climate; it has several, arranged from south to north.\n- Mount Cameroon is in the South West, near Buea and Limbe.\n- Do not confuse the Wouri (Douala) with the Sanaga (Edea).\n- 'Africa in miniature' is a description of variety, not of size.")],
    [("Example 1: explain a climate contrast", "Why is the Far North of Cameroon much drier than the South?", ["The south is close to the equator and the Atlantic, so moist air and convectional rain are frequent.", "The Far North is far from the sea and close to the Sahara, with a short rainy season.", "Therefore the rainy season is short and rainfall small."], "Because it is far from the sea and near the Sahara, so it has a short rainy season."),
     ("Example 2: identify a region from clues", "A region has volcanic soils, mountains above 2 000 m, a cool climate and dense population. Which relief region is it?", ["Volcanic mountains with cool climate suggest highlands.", "Fertile volcanic soil attracts farmers and a dense population.", "This is the western highlands."], "The western highlands.")],
    (fig, "Natural regions from north to south (schematic)", "Four horizontal bands showing the Far North, the North, the highlands and plateau, and the south."),
    [MCQ("Which country is Cameroon's neighbour to the west?", "Nigeria", ["Gabon", "Chad", "Congo"], "Nigeria borders Cameroon on the west."),
     TF("Cameroon has ten regions.", True, "Adamawa, Centre, East, Far North, Littoral, North, North West, South, South West and West."),
     MATCH("Match each river with where it flows.", [("Sanaga", "Atlantic Ocean"), ("Logone", "Lake Chad"), ("Benue", "River Niger")], "These rivers drain to different basins."),
     MCQ("Mount Cameroon is in the", "South West Region", ["Far North Region", "East Region", "Adamawa Region"], "It stands near Buea.", tier="approfondissement"),
     OPEN("Explain why Cameroon is called 'Africa in miniature'.", "Because it has many of the continent's landscapes and climates in one country: equatorial forest, savanna, semi-desert, mountains, a coast, and also many ethnic groups and languages.", "2 marks for variety of landscape/climate; 1 mark for examples; 1 mark for people if mentioned.", points=3, tier="approfondissement"),
     PROB("Study the following description of a journey from Douala to Maroua: forest and plantations; then a plateau and grassland; then dry savanna and thorn bushes.",
          [("mcq", "The direction of the journey is mainly", "north", ["south", "west", "east"], "Maroua is in the Far North, so the journey is northwards.", {}),
           ("tf", "The amount of rainfall increases as the journey goes north.", False, "Rainfall decreases towards the north.", {}),
           ("mcq", "The thorn bushes are typical of the", "Sahel zone", ["equatorial forest", "mangrove coast", "mountain peaks"], "Thorn shrubs are typical of the Sahel.", {}),
           ("open", "Explain one way in which climate affects farming along this journey.", "In the south heavy rain allows tree crops like cocoa and banana; in the drier north, farmers grow cotton and millet and herd cattle, and the long dry season limits what can be grown.", "1 mark for the north/south contrast; 1 mark for a crop example.", {})])],
    [("The longest river in Cameroon is the", "Sanaga", ["Wouri", "Ntem", "Benue"], "The Sanaga is the longest river wholly within the country (to be verified in the notes)."),
     ("The capital of Cameroon is", "Yaoundé", ["Douala", "Garoua", "Buea"], "Yaoundé is the political capital."),
     ("The Adamawa plateau lies in the", "Centre of the country", ["Far North corner", "Coastal strip", "South West"], "It is in the centre-north."),
     ("The Sahel climate has", "A short rainy season", ["Rain all year", "No dry season", "Snow in winter"], "Rainfall is limited and unreliable."),
     ("A river flowing into Lake Chad is the", "Logone", ["Sanaga", "Nyong", "Ntem"], "The Logone drains to the Chad basin.")],
    ["Facts to verify: the area (about 475 000 km²), the ten regions, plateau altitudes (about 650 m and 1 000 m), the Sanaga as the longest river entirely in Cameroon, the Logone/Sangha drainage, and the triangle shape. Climate zone names should be checked against the textbook used for the syllabus."])

